  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pierogi use a rested, pliable dough that is easy to roll and easy to seal. Fill each round, "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "crimp",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "dumpling-crimp"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " tightly, boil until they float, then pan-fry in butter for colour and texture. Makes about 30."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The classic filling uses mashed potato and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "curd cheese ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "curd-cheese"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Use a firm, dry curd rather than a wet ricotta so the filling holds its shape."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "plain-flour",
              "amount": 400,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "plus extra for dusting",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "dough"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "soured-cream",
              "amount": 200,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "full fat",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "dough"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "eggs",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "dough"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "potato",
              "amount": 600,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "peeled, boiled and mashed",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "filling"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "onion",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": "finely diced and softened in butter",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "filling"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "unsalted-butter",
              "amount": 60,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "divided",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "soured-cream",
              "amount": 4,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": "to serve",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "to serve"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mix the flour, sour cream, and egg together in a bowl until a soft dough forms. Knead for 5 minutes until smooth. Wrap and rest for 30 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cook the onion in 20g of the butter over low heat for 10 minutes until very soft. Mix into the mashed potato with seasoning. Allow to cool completely."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Roll the dough out on a floured surface to 3mm thickness. Cut out rounds using an 8cm cutter or glass. Place a heaped teaspoon of filling in the centre of each round. Fold over and press the edges firmly together. Crimp the edge with a fork or your fingers."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Bring a large pan of water to a boil. Cook the pierogi in batches for 3 to 4 minutes until they float to the surface and the dough is cooked through. Remove with a slotted spoon."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Melt the remaining butter in a frying pan over medium-high heat. Fry the boiled pierogi in batches for 1 to 2 minutes per side until golden. Serve immediately with sour cream."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Pierogi burst open while boiling"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The edges were not sealed properly. Press firmly and use a fork to crimp. Make sure there is no filling on the dough edge before sealing."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Dough is tough"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The dough was worked too much after resting, or it was not rested long enough. Give it the full 30 minutes and handle gently."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Filling is too wet"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mash the potato dry with no added liquid. If using curd cheese, drain it overnight in a sieve to remove excess moisture."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pierogi are the defining dish of Polish home cooking, made for Sunday dinners, Christmas Eve, and family gatherings. The potato and cheese filling is the most common, but versions with meat, sauerkraut, or sweet cherries also exist. They take time to make but the process is satisfying and the results freeze beautifully."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
